\section{Conclusion}

This paper focuses on the co-adaption problem of deep self-attention networks, and presents a novel dropout method onto self-attention empowered pre-trained language models. Extensive experiments on multiple natural language processing tasks demonstrate that our proposed approach is universal and qualified to enable more robust task-specific tuning, which contributes to much stronger state-of-the-arts. We probe into the learned dropout patterns on different tasks, which empirically guide us to the very needed dynamic attention dropout design.


